{"base_rate":0.4287652645861601,"brier":0.18829077340569877,"bss":0.23123281592952272,"bss_hi":0.33467507780182115,"bss_lo":0.11191034574157066,"chart":{"base":[432.6,182.5],"fp":[419.0,202.0],"lead":"62,168.6 272,160.2 482,145.3 692,105.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.23 — higher than 35% of cities","fp":"low end +13pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.9 °C — better than 7% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 12%; promised 100% → rained 84%"},"rel":"70.2,414.8 276.4,286.5 586.5,192.7 689.7,103.6"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13396200814111264,"ess":340.63352723426726,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Newcastle</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Newcastle rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNEWCASTLE NOBBYS SIGNAL STATIO, 2.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.23, ranked 141 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(85&ndash;175) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>201</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>149</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Newcastle</b> <span class=\"muted\">Australia</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;43% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 43% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.23</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>85&ndash;175\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Newcastle &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Newcastle\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.10567164179105,380.18905472636817 73.06558139534884,352.266279069768 130.52575000000002,277.35 230.26405405405407,165.56756756756755 324.3208695652173,76.02898550724638 377.8253846153846,32.0 410.6932885906041,18.0 410.6932885906041,22.885906040268424 377.8253846153846,78.66666666666663 324.3208695652173,144.6086956521739 230.26405405405407,244.27027027027026 130.52575000000002,336.5 73.06558139534884,377.7674418604651 58.10567164179105,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"225.92944369063773\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"225.92944369063773\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.10567164179105,351.2139303482587 73.06558139534884,310.04651162790697 130.52575000000002,245.5 230.26405405405407,214.75675675675674 324.3208695652173,139.33333333333334 377.8253846153846,162.66666666666669 410.6932885906041,76.63087248322148\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 201 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.10567164179105\" cy=\"351.2139303482587\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"73.06558139534884\" cy=\"310.04651162790697\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"130.52575000000002\" cy=\"245.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 49%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"230.26405405405407\" cy=\"214.75675675675674\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"324.3208695652173\" cy=\"139.33333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.8253846153846\" cy=\"162.66666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 149 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.6932885906041\" cy=\"76.63087248322148\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(43%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Newcastle the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.27) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.024</td><td class='num'>18.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>202</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.256</td><td class='num'>12.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.266</td><td class='num'>12.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.273</td><td class='num'>11.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-32.92953,"lon":151.7801,"n":737,"n_cities":216,"name":"Newcastle","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00029850746268656717,"n":201,"obs":0.0845771144278607,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.04255813953488373,"n":86,"obs":0.19767441860465115,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.204875,"n":80,"obs":0.375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.65,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.4866216216216217,"n":74,"obs":0.4594594594594595,"sig":false},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.65,"mean":0.75231884057971,"n":69,"obs":0.6666666666666666,"sig":false},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9034615384615384,"n":78,"obs":0.6025641025641025,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.9963087248322149,"n":149,"obs":0.8389261744966443,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.1,"provisional":false,"rank":141,"rank_hi":175.0,"rank_lo":85.0,"reliability":0.023237199368296785,"resolution":0.08145593673433887,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"newcastle","station":"NEWCASTLE NOBBYS SIGNAL STATIO","timezone